# Imports: Barrel Only, One Line Per Module

**Barrel paths only.** When importing from constants, types, utils, hooks, or services, use the **top-level barrel** only. Do not use subpaths.

- **✅** `import { COLORS, FONTS } from "@/constants";`
- **❌** `import { COLORS } from "@/constants/colors";` or `import { formatPrice } from "@/utils/formatPrice";`

**One import line per module.** Never use two or more import statements from the same module. Combine into one.

- **✅** `import { COLORS, FONTS, ASSETS } from "@/constants";`
- **❌** Two lines: `import { COLORS } from "@/constants";` and `import { FONTS } from "@/constants";`

Source: `docs/import-patterns-guide.md` (Use Barrel Paths Only, One Import Line Per Module).
